// EMIR -- Calibre PEX statements, a SKETCH. UNVERIFIED: never run (no Calibre
// where EMIR was developed). See NOTES.md for what each line is meant to give
// EMIR's DSPF reader, and check every statement against your release.
//
// One run per kind, from ONE LVS database:
//   R      -> ${CELL}.r_only.dspf       the grid `emir run` screens with DC currents
//   RCC    -> ${CELL}.rc_coupled.dspf   the RC netlist rcc simulates and screens

PEX NETLIST "${CELL}.r_only.dspf" DSPF SOURCENAMES
PEX REDUCE ANALOG NO
// resistor annotations EMIR needs: width, length, layer, location (UNVERIFIED
// that these annotate a DSPF; the public material shows them for CALIBREVIEW)
// PEX NETLIST ... RWIDTH RLENGTH RLAYER RLOCATION
